# Chrome Extension Architecture (MV3)

## Component Boundaries

- **Popup** (`popup.js`): UI, orchestration, storage reads/writes, tab navigation. Never touches LinkedIn DOM.
- **Content script** (`content.js`): LinkedIn DOM only — scroll, expand, extract. Never renders popup UI.
- **Service worker** (`background.js`): Lifecycle events, tab cleanup, popup auto-open. No DOM access.

## Rules

- No external network requests (`fetch`, XHR, WebSocket) in any module
- Cross-context communication via `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` or `chrome.tabs.sendMessage` only
- Content script uses IIFE with `__linkedinEmailCollectorInitialized` guard
- Settings live in popup Settings view — no separate options page
- New features must declare which execution context owns the logic

## Message Flow

```
popup → tabs.sendMessage → content (DOM operations)
popup → runtime.sendMessage → background (tab lifecycle)
content → sendResponse → popup (results only)
```

Do not add background → content direct messaging without documenting in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
